<article class="env-proposition" id="02QK">
<p><a class="environment-identifier" href="/tag/02QK">Proposition <span data-tag="02QK">9.7.2.6</span>.</a> Let $f: K \rightarrow K'$ be a categorical equivalence of simplicial sets. Then $K$ is sifted if and only if $K'$ is sifted. </p>
</article><article class="env-proof">
<p>
<strong>Proof.</strong>
      It will suffice to show that, for every finite set $I$, the diagonal map $\delta _{K}: K \rightarrow K^{I}$ is right cofinal if and only if the diagonal map $\delta _{K'}: K' \rightarrow K'^{I}$ is right cofinal. This follows by applying Corollary <a data-tag="02NN" href="/tag/02NN">7.2.1.22</a> to the commutative diagram 
    <p>
<div class="equation">
  \[  \xymatrix@R =50pt@C=50pt{ K \ar [r]^-{\delta _{K}} \ar [d]^{f} &amp;  K^{I} \ar [d]^{f^{I}} \\ K' \ar [r]^-{\delta _{K'}} &amp;  K'^{I}. } \]
</div>
<span class="qed">$\square$</span>
</p>
</p></article>
